roic_consistency":null,"_score_roic_consistency":null,"_gate_incr_roic":null,"_gp_incr_roic":null,"_score_incr_roic":null,"_gate_margin_advantage":null,"_gp_margin_advantage":null,"_score_margin_advantage":null,"_gate_pool_share":-0.017827335711855907,"_gp_pool_share":false,"_score_pool_share":32.9,"_gate_rev_durability":0.12304705972769825,"_gp_rev_durability":true,"_score_rev_durability":86.5,"_gate_fcf_durability":null,"_gp_fcf_durability":null,"_score_fcf_durability":null,"_gate_margins":null,"_gp_margins":null,"_score_margins":null,"_gate_fund_growth":null,"_gp_fund_growth":null,"_score_fund_growth":null,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.01628906022467443,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":false,"_score_shrhldr_yield":29.2,"_gate_share_shrink":0.0016338340615509317,"_gp_share_shrink":false,"_score_share_shrink":48.0,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.0052575338130366215,"_gp_sbc_dilution":true,"_score_sbc_dilution":91.2,"_gate_insider_own":0.065409996,"_gp_insider_own":true,"_score_insider_own":43.6,"_gate_insider_buying":null,"_gp_insider_buying":null,"_score_insider_buying":null,"pf":[],"description_full":"ServisFirst Bancshares, Inc. operates as the bank holding company for ServisFirst Bank that provides banking services to individual and corporate customers in the United States. It offers deposit services, including checking, money market, savings, and individual retirement arrangements (IRA) accounts, as well as certificates of deposit. The company also provides real estate loans that consist of commercial real estate loans, 1-4 family residential real estate loans, and construction and development loans; consumer loans, such as home equity loans, vehicle financing, loans secured by deposits, and secured and unsecured personal loans; and commercial loans comprising seasonal, bridge, and term loans, as well as commercial lines of credit. In addition, it offers other banking services, such as 24-hour telephone banking, direct deposit, Internet banking, mobile banking, traveler's checks, safe deposit boxes, attorney trust accounts, and automatic account transfers, as well as automated teller machines and debit and credit card systems. Further, the company provides treasury and cash management services; direct deposit, wire transfer, night depository, banking-by-mail and remote capture services for non-cash items; and correspondent banking services to other financial institutions. Additionally, it holds and manages participations in residential mortgages and commercial real estate loans originated by ServisFirst Bank in Alabama, Florida, Georgia, and Tennessee. ServisFirst Bancshares, Inc. was founded in 2005 and is headquartered in Birmingham, Alabama.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Thomas Ashford Broughton III | Chairman, President & CEO | Age 70 | Compensation: $1.7M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 683 people. Revenue per employee of $823K ranks in the above the sector median among Financial Services peers, improving at 15%/yr \u2014 growing workforce leverage. Stock-based compensation of $4K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 2\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (5/10).","financial_summary":["ServisFirst Bancshares, Inc. is a mid-cap financial services business with a $4.5B market cap on $562M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +4% over the past three years and +12% annually across the full decade, which puts it in mature, slow-growth territory.","Returns on capital run at 16% against a 9% cost of capital, a 7-point spread that creates value, though narrow enough that competitive pressure could close it.","On the balance sheet, leverage is comfortably conservative at 0.0\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and thin 0.8\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield is only 1.6%, a thin return of capital, and insiders hold 6.5% of the shares, and within its sector the business captures 2.3\u00d7 its fair share of profits, a structural advantage visible in the numbers."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (0.4) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Price sits 15% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left","sev":"amber","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.15347694590150532},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 6.3% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Significant insider selling (net $4.2M)","sev":"amber","cat":"insider","dollars":-4157445.0},{"text":"Above-average market volatility (VIX 26)","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Late-cycle dynamics increase the probability of a slowdown","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Credit cycles and regulatory capital \u2014 losses accumulate invisibly in good years and appear all at once, and the time to worry is when underwriting standards are loosest.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Fintech disintermediation \u2014 neobanks, embedded finance, and blockchain rails are unbundling the fee streams that traditional banks took for granted.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Interest rate regime shifts \u2014 a rapid move in rates can invert the yield curve, crush bond portfolios, and trigger deposit flight simultaneously.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Operating margins 32% above sector median \u2014 the quantitative trace of pricing power","11 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 an operating record that makes the dividend claim credible","Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment","Minimal goodwill on the balance sheet \u2014 low impairment risk"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Financial Contrast: ServisFirst Bancshares (NYSE:SFBS) & TrustCo Bank Corp NY (NASDAQ:TRST)","source":"